1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,984
Every popcorn kernel is a tiny pressure cooker.

2
00:00:03,214 --> 00:00:04,556
And every single one

3
00:00:04,576 --> 00:00:06,588
is counting down to an explosion.

4
00:00:07,188 --> 00:00:09,151
Most people think heat just makes

5
00:00:09,171 --> 00:00:10,563
the corn burst open.

6
00:00:10,793 --> 00:00:13,116
But the real trick is hiding inside.

7
00:00:13,716 --> 00:00:16,300
Each kernel holds a tiny drop of water,

8
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,283
about fourteen percent of its weight,

9
00:00:18,303 --> 00:00:19,694
packed into soft starch.

10
00:00:19,924 --> 00:00:21,887
Around it sits a hard shell

11
00:00:21,907 --> 00:00:23,609
that barely lets anything out.

12
00:00:24,209 --> 00:00:25,241
Heat it up,

13
00:00:25,261 --> 00:00:27,274
and that water turns into steam.

14
00:00:27,504 --> 00:00:28,895
The shell traps it.

15
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:31,088
Pressure climbs to nearly ten times

16
00:00:31,108 --> 00:00:32,140
normal air pressure,

17
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,812
while the starch inside softens

18
00:00:33,832 --> 00:00:35,224
into a hot gel.

19
00:00:35,824 --> 00:00:38,097
At around one hundred eighty degrees Celsius,

20
00:00:38,117 --> 00:00:39,819
the shell finally gives up.

21
00:00:40,419 --> 00:00:41,761
In a split second,

22
00:00:41,781 --> 00:00:43,123
the steam rushes out

23
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:45,416
and puffs the gel into a foam,

24
00:00:45,436 --> 00:00:47,139
up to forty times bigger.

25
00:00:47,369 --> 00:00:48,710
It cools almost instantly

26
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:51,054
and sets into that crunchy white cloud.

27
00:00:51,654 --> 00:00:53,356
And the pop you hear?

28
00:00:53,586 --> 00:00:54,928
Scientists filmed it at

29
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:56,650
thousands of frames per second.

30
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:59,153
The sound comes from the steam escaping,

31
00:00:59,173 --> 00:01:00,876
not from the shell cracking.

32
00:01:01,106 --> 00:01:02,758
Even the jump is wild:

33
00:01:02,778 --> 00:01:04,430
a little leg of starch

34
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:06,463
kicks the kernel into the air.

35
00:01:07,063 --> 00:01:08,765
The kernels that never pop?

36
00:01:08,995 --> 00:01:11,008
Usually a damaged or dried-out shell.

37
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,580
The steam leaks away,

38
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,302
so the pressure never builds.

39
00:01:14,902 --> 00:01:17,175
One drop of water, one tough shell,

40
00:01:17,195 --> 00:01:18,277
one tiny explosion.

41
00:01:18,507 --> 00:01:19,538
What everyday thing

42
00:01:19,558 --> 00:01:20,950
should we unpack next?
